p.src:
The leading example is the environment, especially the prevention of extinction. The Nature Conservancy is introduced not as ornament but as a model of numerate, organized, mission-driven finance. Its lecture-time scale is given by $\begin{aligned}
\text{assets} &\approx \$5.6 \text{ billion},\\
\text{land protected} &\approx 500{,}000\ \text{km}^2,\\
\text{world land area} &\approx 150{,}000{,}000\ \text{km}^2.\end{aligned}$ From these quantities Shiller performs a small but telling calculation: $\frac{500{,}000}{150{,}000{,}000}
=
\frac{1}{300}
\approx 0.0033
\approx 0.33\%.$ That is his one-third of one percent of world land protected.

